VERDICT: REJECTED — Precision gate FAILED (confirmed after harness fix)

========================================
HARNESS BUG FIXED
========================================
Previous commit d097337f contained a critical use-after-free bug in
run_correctness_shape():

    cudaMemcpy(hC_gpu, dC, ...);
    delete[] hA; delete[] hB; delete[] hC_ref; delete[] hC_gpu;  // FREED HERE
    cudaFree(...);
    for (...) {
        float ref = hC_ref[i];   // USE AFTER FREE
        float cmp = hC_gpu[i];   // USE AFTER FREE
    }

This undefined behavior produced wildly varying max_rel values
(1.66 in one run, ~1e12 in another) and invalidated the original
precision verdict.

FIX APPLIED: Move evaluation BEFORE any free/delete. The corrected
order is now:

1. cudaMemcpy dC -> hC_gpu
2. Evaluate ALL correctness metrics using live hC_ref and hC_gpu
3. Print/store result
4. Only THEN: delete[] hA, hB, hC_ref, hC_gpu; cudaFree dA/dB/dC

Also fixed harmless printf warning: %zu now receives (size_t)M*N.

